{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-psalms-069",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 69,
  "title": "Psalms 69",
  "display_title": "Psalms 69",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "psalms",
  "book": "Psalms",
  "bookName": "Psalms",
  "bookOrder": 19,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 69,
  "sortOrder": 19069,
  "verseCount": 36,
  "aliases": [
    "Psalm",
    "Psalms",
    "Ps",
    "Psa",
    "Psm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Save me, O God; for the waters are come in unto my soul.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "I sink in deep mire, where there is no standing: I am come into deep waters, where the floods overflow me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "I am weary of my crying: my throat is dried: mine eyes fail while I wait for my God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "They that hate me without a cause are more than the hairs of mine head: they that would destroy me, being mine enemies wrongfully, are mighty: then I restored that which I took not away.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "O God, thou knowest my foolishness; and my sins are not hid from thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Let not them that wait on thee, O Lord GOD of hosts, be ashamed for my sake: let not those that seek thee be confounded for my sake, O God of Israel.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Because for thy sake I have borne reproach; shame hath covered my face.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "I am become a stranger unto my brethren, and an alien unto my mother’s children.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "For the zeal of thine house hath eaten me up; and the reproaches of them that reproached thee are fallen upon me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "When I wept, and chastened my soul with fasting, that was to my reproach.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "I made sackcloth also my garment; and I became a proverb to them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "They that sit in the gate speak against me; and I was the song of the drunkards.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "But as for me, my prayer is unto thee, O LORD, in an acceptable time: O God, in the multitude of thy mercy hear me, in the truth of thy salvation.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Deliver me out of the mire, and let me not sink: let me be delivered from them that hate me, and out of the deep waters.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Let not the waterflood overflow me, neither let the deep swallow me up, and let not the pit shut her mouth upon me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Hear me, O LORD; for thy lovingkindness is good: turn unto me according to the multitude of thy tender mercies.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "And hide not thy face from thy servant; for I am in trouble: hear me speedily.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Draw nigh unto my soul, and redeem it: deliver me because of mine enemies.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Thou hast known my reproach, and my shame, and my dishonour: mine adversaries are all before thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Reproach hath broken my heart; and I am full of heaviness: and I looked for some to take pity, but there was none; and for comforters, but I found none.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "They gave me also gall for my meat; and in my thirst they gave me vinegar to drink.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Let their table become a snare before them: and that which should have been for their welfare, let it become a trap.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Let their eyes be darkened, that they see not; and make their loins continually to shake.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Pour out thine indignation upon them, and let thy wrathful anger take hold of them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "Let their habitation be desolate; and let none dwell in their tents.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "For they persecute him whom thou hast smitten; and they talk to the grief of those whom thou hast wounded.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "Add iniquity unto their iniquity: and let them not come into thy righteousness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "Let them be blotted out of the book of the living, and not be written with the righteous.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "But I am poor and sorrowful: let thy salvation, O God, set me up on high.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "I will praise the name of God with a song, and will magnify him with thanksgiving.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "This also shall please the LORD better than an ox or bullock that hath horns and hoofs.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "The humble shall see this, and be glad: and your heart shall live that seek God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "For the LORD heareth the poor, and despiseth not his prisoners.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-034",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 34,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:34",
      "numberLabel": "34",
      "text": "Let the heaven and earth praise him, the seas, and every thing that moveth therein.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:34",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:34"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-035",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 35,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:35",
      "numberLabel": "35",
      "text": "For God will save Zion, and will build the cities of Judah: that they may dwell there, and have it in possession.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:35",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:35"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-036",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 36,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:69:36",
      "numberLabel": "36",
      "text": "The seed also of his servants shall inherit it: and they that love his name shall dwell therein.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 69:36",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:69:36"
      }
    }
  ],
